Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 06:22:36 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 14/14] Document \caption* in usrguide; draft LaTeX News
 entries

This commit is meant to be applied last and only when hyperref supports
\caption*: hyperref without \DocumentMetadata, the most common setup,
replaces \caption, so \caption* still gives a numbered caption with
the text "*". The change asked of hyperref, when \@kernel@caption is
defined: keep its \caption for numbered captions, pass only the star to
\@kernel@caption*, and start each numbered caption with
\@kernel@caption@reset. (Not patching the caption commands at all,
\hyper@nopatch@caption, was tested and is not proposed: it gives
duplicate destinations with mwart, and the nameref title of a caption
would then have to come from the kernel.)

usrguide gets the section "Captions without a number" (with a source
comment that says this) and clsguide refers to it. ltnews44 gets draft
entries for the caption interface: "Captions in tagged floats" (with
latex3/latex2e#2022), "Captions without a number: \caption*", "Hooks and
sockets for floats and captions", "\caption outside a float" and
"\caption* with the float package". They assume the 2026-11-01 release,
the placeholder date of the \IncludeInRelease blocks; the sentences on
the socket caption/typeset, the copy \@kernel@@caption and the sub-float
sockets are marked as requests for comments. The team may prefer to
write LaTeX News itself; then only the usrguide part is needed.

ltnews44, usrguide and clsguide typeset without errors.
