+% caption interface (tagging)
+\subsection{Captions in tagged floats}
+
+The tagging code for floats no longer redefines \cs{caption}; it uses the
+new caption interface of the kernel (see below), and it now stores the
+link target of a float in \cs{@floatHref@}\meta{type}. Before, the
+second caption of a float split with the \key{float/split} key and a
+\texttt{table} caption inside a \texttt{figure} referred to link targets
+that did not exist.
+
+Float types that are not known to the tagging code now get generic
+structure names for their captions and labels, and packages that define
+float environments can declare their types with
+\cs{DeclareTaggingFloatType}\Arg{type}. The contract of the socket
+\texttt{caption/label} is now documented, and a new socket
+\texttt{caption/separator} allows the separator after the label to be
+tagged as part of the caption text instead of the label. A label that
+prints nothing no longer gives unbalanced paragraph tags in a wide
+caption.
+\githubissue{2022}
+%
+% request for comments (sub-float sockets):
+The new tagging sockets \texttt{subfloat/box}, \texttt{subfloat/begin} and
+\texttt{subfloat/end} let packages such as \pkg{subcaption} tag a
+sub-figure or sub-table as a \struct{Part} with its own caption.
+
+
+
