+% caption interface (\caption*)
+\subsection{Captions without a number: \cs{caption*}}
+
+Where \cs{caption} can be used, \cs{caption*}\texttt{[}\meta{opt}\texttt{]}\Arg{text} now
+typesets \meta{text} as a caption without a label: the counter is not
+stepped, nothing is written to the list of figures or tables, and no link
+target is made. The caption has the layout of the document class: the
+class's \cs{@makecaption} is called with a label that prints nothing and
+removes a colon or a period and the space after it, so the standard
+classes and many classes derived from them need no change. Classes that
+print the separator in some other way can test the new switch
+\cs{if@captionstar}; \texttt{clsguide} describes what they should do.
+Packages and classes that replace \cs{caption} itself (for example
+\pkg{hyperref} without \cs{DocumentMetadata}, or \cls{beamer}) do not
+support the star form and give a numbered caption with the text `*', as
+before.
+
+
+% caption interface (hooks and sockets)
+\subsection{Hooks and sockets for floats and captions}
+
+Packages that change floats or captions had to redefine internal
+commands such as \cs{@xfloat}, \cs{caption} or \cs{@caption}, which made
+them hard to combine. The kernel now provides
+\begin{itemize}
+\item the hooks \hook{float/begin} and \hook{float/end}, executed inside
+  the box of every float, with the float type and a star for
+  double-column floats as arguments;
+\item the hook \hook{caption/before}, executed after \cs{caption} has
+  read its arguments and before the counter is stepped, and the hook
+  \hook{caption/prepare}, executed by \cs{@caption} for every caption
+  once \cs{@currentlabel} is set;
+\item the sockets \texttt{caption/step} (stepping the counter and making
+  the link target) and \texttt{caption/listentry} (the entry in the list
+  of figures, tables, etc.);
+\item \cs{@kernel@caption}, a copy of the kernel \cs{caption}, for code
+  that keeps its own \cs{caption} and passes \cs{caption*} to the
+  kernel (it is also the test whether the interface is there);
+% request for comments (caption/typeset, \@kernel@@caption):
+\item the socket \texttt{caption/typeset}, and the copy
+  \cs{@kernel@@caption} of the kernel \cs{@caption}, so that a package
+  that has always replaced \cs{caption} and \cs{@caption} can restore
+  both and use the hooks and sockets instead.
+\end{itemize}
+With the default plugs the output does not change. A caption whose
+counter is not stepped (for example the caption of a continued float)
+gets the target of its float or a target with a unique name, never a
+second target with the name of the previous caption. The interface is
+described in \texttt{ltfloat.dtx}.
+
+
+
